;; The reference host's DejaGnu target and effective targets (doc/C23-SURVEY.md, "As built: CS140-CS144, CS146"; CS142 (a)): what
;; gcc's `target` and `xfail` selectors in the C23 corpus's directives mean on the host the references are built on, read
;; by arbace.c.dg. Recorded from `gcc -dumpmachine` and from probes with gcc 15.2.0 -std=c23 (a file with `_Decimal32`,
;; `__int128`, `_BitInt (575)`, `_BitInt (65535)`, `_Float16`, `_Float32` and `__builtin_inff ()` compiles; INT_MAX is at
;; least 2147483647). A name not listed here is taken to hold in dg-do, dg-error and xfail selectors (the judge's earlier
;; rule); in a dg-options line's selector it is unknown, the line kept and reported (review 027, finding 5: the names of
;; the corpora's option selectors listed, ia32 false as __i386__ is not defined, fpic true as -fpic compiles, signal true
;; on Linux, newlib_nano_io false with musl). The C++ names do not hold.
{:triple "x86_64-alpine-linux-musl"
 :effective {"c" true "c++" false "c++11" false "c++98_only" false "c++17" false
             "dfp" true "inff" true "int128" true "int32plus" true
             "bitint" true "bitint128" true "bitint575" true "bitint65535" true
             "float32" true "float16_runtime" true "exceptions" true
             "fstack_protector" true "lto" true "native" true
             "ia32" false "fpic" true "signal" true "newlib_nano_io" false}}
